    "bookTitle": "2 Kings",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 17,
    "summary": "Hoshea reigns in Israel and is subject to the Assyrians—The Israelites forsake the Lord, worship idols, serve Baal, and reject all that the Lord has given them—The ten tribes are carried away captive by the kings of Assyria—The land of Israel (Samaria) is repopulated by other people—Many forms of false worship are found among the Samaritans.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of Judah began Hoshea the son of Elah to reign in Samaria over Israel nine years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Kings 17:1",
        "book": "2 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And he did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord, but not as the kings of Israel that were before him.",
